# Osler Admin — build-time GitHub OAuth configuration
#
# client_id  = PUBLIC. Safe to commit, safe to ship in the binary.
# client_secret = ONLY needed if your OAuth App is registered as CONFIDENTIAL.
#                Keep this in a gitignored .env (never commit it). For public
#                releases, register the app as a public client so no secret is
#                required.
#
# To use the preconfigured Osler GitHub sign-in (zero setup for end users):
#   1. Create an OAuth App at https://github.com/settings/developers
#   2. Set the Authorization callback URL to: http://localhost:7878/callback
#   3. Paste the client_id below (and client_secret if the app is confidential).
#   4. Rebuild the app (`cargo build` / `npm run tauri:build`).
#
# If you leave both blank, users must enter their own client_id in the app
# (Settings → GitHub, or the setup wizard's GitHub sign-in step).
GH_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GH_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
